# Chicken corn soup (for when someone has a cold)

- 500 g chicken with bones, 8 cups water, 1 tsp salt, ginger slice
- 1 can cream-style corn
- 2 eggs, beaten
- 3 tbsp cornflour in ½ cup water
- white pepper, soy sauce, chilli vinegar to serve

Boil the chicken 40 minutes, shred the meat, strain the stock. Add corn and shredded chicken, bring back to a boil, stir in the cornflour slurry until it thickens. Turn the heat down and drizzle the egg in a thin stream while stirring slowly so it forms ribbons.

Everyone adds their own vinegar and pepper at the table.
